Where do we see a nested call here? It seems like we're just performing two calls in succession. Would it be more helpful to test something like the following? (which fails in a weird way on [main](https://play.ty.dev/68eaf6c4-a993-4783-85e6-a70dbaae2d8c)):
```py
class Container[T]:
    value: T

    def __init__(self, value: T):
        self.value = value

    def wrapped(self) -> Container[Container[T]]:
        return Container(self)
```

